WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.940
The Vision and Scarlet Witch have had an interesting
romantic relationship, both in the movies

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.170
and in comics. However, there’s a lot of
weird stuff about their love affair that nobody

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:13.830
seems to talk about. These are just a few
of the weirdest, wackiest, and most disturbing

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.480
things about Scarlet Witch and Vision’s
relationship.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.400
Might as well get this out of the way immediately:
The Vision is a robot. He was created by another

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.300
robot, the villainous Ultron, who had the
intent of using him to destroy the Avengers.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:31.240
In the comics, Vision has variously been described
as an android and as a synthezoid, but he's

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:37.510
never described as being a human. Because,
well, he's not. He's a machine. Scarlet Witch,

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:42.060
aka Wanda Maximoff, is not a robot. She's
a human being and there's nothing mechanical

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.580
about her. So how can a human and a robot
be involved in a romantic relationship? Is

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.940
a robot even capable of giving consent to
such an arrangement?

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.540
In the comics, Vision has long held a desire
to know what it means to become human. It's

00:00:54.541 --> 00:00:58.190
part of what drives him to become involved
with Scarlet Witch to begin with. But he'll

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.500
never be human, and no matter how closely
his mainframe mimics a human being's thoughts

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:07.320
and feelings, he's still severely lacking
in the emotions department. As for Scarlet

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.660
Witch, she bonds with Vision because both
of them are outcasts among their fellow Avengers.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.700
And while she might think she's found a kindred
spirit in Vision, what she's really feeling

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.680
is, in a word, artificial even if she succeeds
in tricking herself into thinking their relationship

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.680
makes sense.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.420
"I — I think it… I think it w... "

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:23.920
"It works."

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:24.420
"It works."

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:29.940
The films of the Marvel Cinematic Universe
do a lot of things incredibly well. After

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.890
all, there's a reason why the franchise has
grossed more than double the take of its closest

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:38.220
competitor at the worldwide box office. But
if there's one thing the films haven't done

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.820
a very good job of, that's selling the audience
on Scarlet Witch and Vision's relationship.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.620
While both characters are introduced in Avengers:
Age of Ultron, it isn't until Captain America:

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.690
Civil War that their relationship starts to
develop — and it does so under some pretty

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.320
unsettling circumstances.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.520
One scene in particular that stands out is
when Vision goes to Wanda's room to check

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:01.750
on her. Instead of knocking on her door and
asking to enter like a normal human would

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.689
do, Vision uses his phasing power to simply
coast through her wall without saying a word,

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:06.980
completely barging in on her.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.660
Wanda rightly calls him out on his creepy
behavior, and Vision apologizes and makes

00:02:11.669 --> 00:02:17.340
up for it by later trying to, uh… keep her
from leaving the mansion? He says he's protecting

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.180
her, but that's not his decision to make.
Vision's wanton disregard of Wanda's requests

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:27.319
and his desire to control her actions are
both major red flags. Not exactly boyfriend

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:28.320
material, Wanda.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.239
After the initial awkwardness of Vision's
uncomfortable flirting in Civil War, he and

00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:37.900
Scarlet Witch get into a physical altercation
when she tries to leave the house. Aided by

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:42.109
Hawkeye, who distracts Vision, Wanda uses
her powers to force Vision through numerous

00:02:42.109 --> 00:02:47.069
floors, leaving him trapped so she can escape.
We know he was being a jerk, but still, there's

00:02:47.069 --> 00:02:50.020
no excuse for resorting to that level of violence.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.480
After Wanda flees, she joins Team Cap in opposing
the superhero-restricting Sokovia Accords.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:00.280
Vision, meanwhile, is a being of logic and
not emotion, so he sides with Team Iron Man

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:04.900
in support of the Accords. This leads to a
giant confrontation between the two groups

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:09.620
at a German airport, with Vision and Scarlet
Witch engaging in the battle on opposing sides.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.840
Although the two don't directly fight one
another, they're still using near-lethal force

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.680
against their friends, and either one of them
could have taken the other out by accident.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.419
In fact, this almost happens after Vision
uses his solar beam to cut down a tower in

00:03:22.419 --> 00:03:26.920
an attempt to block the path of the fleeing
Captain America and Winter Soldier. Scarlet

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.930
Witch uses her hex powers to keep the tower
from falling, but it drops anyway after War

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:35.209
Machine hits her with a sonic attack, leaving
her very close to becoming seriously injured

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:40.249
as a result of Vision's initial assault. After
this, the two apologize to each other, but

00:03:40.249 --> 00:03:43.300
that doesn't excuse the fact that they almost
killed each other to begin with.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.959
In the MCU, things between Vision and Scarlet
Witch haven't progressed beyond the point

00:03:47.959 --> 00:03:52.629
of living together, but they go much, much
further in the comics. The duo gets married

00:03:52.629 --> 00:03:58.489
in 1975's Giant-Size Avengers #4 in a dual
ceremony alongside their fellow Avengers,

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:03.120
Mantis and the Swordsman. Technically, it
isn't really the Swordsman, but rather a plant

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.839
alien inhabiting the Swordsman's corpse, making
Vision and Scarlet Witch's wedding only the

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.989
second strangest nuptials to take place that
day. Comic books can be very weird sometimes.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.000
"Well, the heart wants what it wants."

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.870
Speaking of weird, Vision asks Scarlet Witch
to marry him immediately after the two of

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:23.471
them fight and defeat some demons in another
dimension. When accepting his proposal, Wanda

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:29.460
says "Don't you see, love is for souls, not
bodies!" This, of course, makes zero sense.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:34.620
Vision is a synthetic human. The one thing
he definitely has is a body, but he most certainly

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:39.160
does not have a soul in the traditional sense.
We're not really sure what Scarlet Witch was

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:43.970
getting at here, but she unintentionally makes
the argument against marrying Vision. Freudian

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.070
slip? Perhaps...

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:51.320
Okay, so Scarlet Witch, a human, illegally
marries Vision, a robot who may or may not

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:55.680
have the capacity to love or fully understand
entering into a commitment like wedlock. You'd

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.300
think that would be the strangest thing about
this couple, but you'd be wrong because Scarlet

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:05.720
Witch and Vision actually have kids. Yes,
you read that right. A robot man fathers children

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:10.340
with a human woman. Now, without getting into
a biology lesson here, let's just say that

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:14.931
such a feat would be impossible. Humans can't
even mate with other organic species, let

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:19.980
alone machines. But the comics get around
this impossibility by way of… wait for it…

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:20.840
"Magic."

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.910
Scarlet Witch explains to Vision that she
conceived when magic from some defeated witches

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:29.840
was funnelled through her as Vision held her,
saying that while it was happening, she wished

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:35.710
for a child. Yikes. After having a relatively
normal pregnancy, Wanda gives birth to twin

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:41.090
boys, William and Tommy, in 1986's The Vision
and The Scarlet Witch #12 in a story titled

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.720
"Double Sized Climax." You can't make this
stuff up, folks.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:49.780
Just a few years after Scarlet Witch and Vision
defy the odds and have children, those kids

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:53.660
are taken away from them in one of the most
cruel and unusual ways possible. How does

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:56.400
that happen? Easy: they were retconned.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:02.180
In 1989's Avengers West Coast #52, the demon
Mephisto while using a possessed man called

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:08.310
Master Pandemonium as his unwitting pawn — absorbs
the twins into his own body, making them Master

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:13.590
Pandemonium's hands. Comics, everybody. Apparently,
Thomas and William were not actual people.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:17.990
Rather, they were fragments of Mephisto's
soul that had manifested into child-like apparitions

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:22.820
by way of the magic Scarlet Witch used to
get herself pregnant. You know, that old chestnut.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:28.500
For a long time, the status quo remained that
Scarlet Witch and Vision's kids were not real.

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:32.930
This, understandably, caused great strain
on their relationship, and it also had a tremendous

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:37.680
effect on Wanda's life moving forward. The
memory or in some storylines where she was

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:42.460
amnesiac, missing memory of her children drove
Scarlet Witch mad, and at multiple times,

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:47.050
she lashed out with Earth-changing consequences.
At some point, the writers at Marvel must've

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.920
felt bad for her because they decided to pull
another retcon and declare that Scarlet Witch

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:55.920
and Vision's kids existed after all. We know,
we know: Make up your mind already, Marvel!

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:01.270
In the comic series Young Avengers in 2005,
we're introduced to two members of the titular

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:06.440
team: Wiccan — a.k.a. William — and Speed,
real name Thomas. Sound familiar? They're

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.660
both mutants, with Wiccan having similar powers
to Scarlet Witch and Speed having the same

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:15.170
power set as Scarlet Witch's twin brother,
Quicksilver. The two youngsters soon discover

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:18.750
that they're long lost twin brothers, and
not only that, but they claim they're the

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:23.070
same William and Thomas who were the sons
of Scarlet Witch and Vision. After some hemming

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:27.440
and hawing, everyone agrees that they are
the kids of the two Avengers, as it's explained

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:32.160
that Wiccan and Speed are the reincarnated
souls of the long thought-nonexistent, magical

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:37.560
offspring. Can non-existent beings have souls?
In a world where robots can make babies, why

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.060
not?

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:42.900
We already briefly mentioned how Scarlet Witch
has gone a little nuts a few times and done

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:47.430
some pretty bad, reality-warpy stuff that
we don't really have time to get into. Well,

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:51.741
one of those times marked the end of her on-again,
off-again relationship with Vision. After

00:07:51.741 --> 00:07:55.780
losing control of her powers and falling under
the control of the villainous Doctor Doom

00:07:55.780 --> 00:08:01.000
in the 2004 comic book storyline Avengers
Disassembled, Wanda launches a series of attacks

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:05.410
on the Avengers. One of these assaults involves
her taking control of Vision's body and having

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:10.760
him crash a jet into Avengers Mansion. Vision
survives the crash, but Wanda uses her powers

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:14.240
to make She-Hulk rip Vision in half, killing
him once again.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:18.820
Vision is rebuilt, but this event proves to
be the final straw for his relationship with

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:24.150
Wanda. During the 2012 "Avengers vs. X-Men"
storyline, Vision finally gets the chance

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:28.169
to confront Wanda about what she did to him.
He essentially tells her that her actions

00:08:28.169 --> 00:08:32.050
were unforgivable, regardless of the fact
that she wasn't in control of her mind when

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:36.460
she committed them. This marks the end of
the pair's decades-long relationship in the

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:36.960
comics.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:41.520
Oh — that's not wacky enough for you? OK,
let's see what we can scrounge up…

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:43.600
Ready? Here we go.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:47.660
Although his former wife is now out of the
picture, Vision still feels the need for a

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:52.449
relationship as part of his never-ending quest
to become a real boy. And let's face it, getting

00:08:52.449 --> 00:08:58.029
a date is hard enough for a regular guy, let
alone an android with two reincarnated and/or

00:08:58.029 --> 00:09:03.079
imaginary and/or demon kids and an ex-wife
who literally killed him. So what's a Vision

00:09:03.079 --> 00:09:08.709
to do but create himself a new wife in his
own image? And in the 2016 self-titled comic

00:09:08.709 --> 00:09:12.009
book series Vision, that's exactly what he
does.

00:09:12.009 --> 00:09:12.840
"What the f—"

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:18.259
Yup. Vision creates himself a synthezoid wife
named Virginia, and he even uses Wanda's brainwaves

00:09:18.259 --> 00:09:23.170
to do so, effectively giving her the mind
of his ex. He then uses their combined brainwaves

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:27.910
to create two children: son Vin and daughter
Viv. They live in the suburbs, and Vin and

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:32.829
Viv attend school. Everything is great…
for about five seconds. Then the villain Grim

00:09:32.829 --> 00:09:36.680
Reaper invades their home and attacks Viv,
stabbing her through the stomach with his

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:41.110
scythe. He's killed by Virginia, who buries
him in their backyard. Virginia's actions

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:45.149
then lead to the death of Viv's friend from
school when the kid's father attempts to blackmail

00:09:45.149 --> 00:09:49.569
her. He shoots at Virginia, but, thanks to
her abilities, the bullets phase through her

00:09:49.569 --> 00:09:54.171
and, well… they connect with the boy's skull.
From there, things just get worse. Virginia

00:09:54.171 --> 00:09:58.759
kills the family dog that Vision created.
Vin is killed by the Ultron-created android

00:09:58.759 --> 00:10:03.370
Victor Mancha, whom Vision considered a brother.
And finally, Virginia kills herself after

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:07.819
confessing to her crimes. The sole survivor
of the family — aside from Vision himself,

00:10:07.819 --> 00:10:12.420
of course — is his daughter, Viv. She ends
up befriending Scarlet Witch, reuniting with

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:16.470
her dog — repaired in a joint effort by
Wanda and Tony Stark — and continuing her

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:21.480
life as a teenage Synthezoid. The comic ends
with the Vision repairing his wife and promptly

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.060
starting the whole shebang over again.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:28.300
Suddenly, the Vision and Scarlet Witch's relationship
doesn't sound so strange, huh? Raise your

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.180
hand if you're stoked for WandaVision!

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:34.820
Check out one of our newest videos right here!
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:39.019
stuff are coming soon. Subscribe to our YouTube
channel and hit the bell so you don't miss

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:39.880
a single one.

